Changes made in this fork:
  - Renamed the extension to "Plexar Browser Bridge" and rebranded every
    user-visible string (connect page, status page, action title,
    description) to reference Plexar Harness instead of Playwright/MCP.
  - Renamed the internal service worker class (PlaywrightExtension ->
    PlexarBrowserBridge), the tab-group title prefix ("Playwright" ->
    "Plexar"), and the cleanup helper (cleanupStalePlaywrightGroups ->
    cleanupStalePlexarGroups); the connected-tab badge title now reads
    "Connected to Plexar Harness".
  - Replaced the light GitHub Primer color palette (colors.css) and the
    page stylesheet (connect.css) with the Plexar dark theme, sourced from
    packages/client/ui-brand-plexar/src/client/tokens/plexar-tokens.css
    (accent --px-accent).
  - Replaced the upstream icon set with apps/plexar-desktop/ui/mark.png,
    resized to 16/32/48/128px (scripts/make-icons.mjs).
  - Renamed the auth-token bypass environment variable
    (PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_EXTENSION_TOKEN -> PLEXAR_BROWSER_BRIDGE_TOKEN) and the
    version-mismatch README link.
  - Replaced the vite + vite-plugin-static-copy build with a small esbuild
    + hand-rolled HTML/icon copy script (scripts/build.mjs) and a
    dependency-free ZIP writer (scripts/zip.mjs, scripts/pack.mjs), to stay
    within the toolchain already vendored in this monorepo.
  - Pinned the manifest "key" to this fork's own developer key so the
    extension id is stable (cnfgenfphpnhddlefhminclbbjdgkbbd) across
    load-unpacked installs; the Chrome Web Store will assign its own key
    and id on first store upload (see README.md).
  - When a client's connection closes, the tabs the client brought into its
    group (the connect page's tab, tabs it created, popups of its tabs)
    close and the tabs the person dragged in are ungrouped; a group that
    Chrome deleted after its last tab closed is recreated with the same
    style; a connect page whose connection fails closes itself.

The relay<->extension wire protocol (WebSocket connect page URL params
mcpRelayUrl, client, protocolVersion, token; the chrome.* command/event
allow-lists in src/relayConnection.ts) is unchanged from upstream so this
extension stays compatible with the server-side relay
(packages/bundle/plexar/src/browser-bridge/**, forked from
playwright-core's src/tools/mcp/cdpRelay.ts / cdpRelayV2.ts /
extensionContextFactory.ts).
